r","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and June to July came in under 90% of normal in 26 of 75 years while February to March and October to November each did it in 37. In 2025 the middle saw October to November at 68% of normal and February to March at 141%. So far in 2026, January to February sat at 53% and April to May at 66% on the middle. Every grid had its driest year in 1976, at 47% or 48% of normal.</p>"}
